  "cli_result_text": "Submitted. Summary of what these files establish for the regression:\n\n**Babel side** (`packages/babel-plugin-proposal-decorators/src/index.ts`): dispatches on `options.legacy`/`options.version` \u2014 `legacy: true` routes to `transformer-legacy.ts` (TS \"experimentalDecorators\" semantics, builds `applyDecoratedDescriptor`/class-decorator calls but **emits no `Reflect.metadata` calls itself**); any `2018-09`+ value routes to the stage-3 implementation in `babel-helper-create-class-features-plugin/src/decorators.ts`. `babel-preset-typescript/src/index.ts` puts `plugin-transform-typescript` in the same plugin array as decorators-legacy for a NestJS-style `.babelrc`; Babel's plugin-pass-per-visitor-key model means both plugins effectively traverse together, and `plugin-transform-typescript/src/index.ts` strips type annotations while leaving `.decorators`/parameter-type metadata usable by the (separately configured) `babel-plugin-transform-typescript-metadata`/`emitDecoratorMetadata`-style plugin most NestJS Babel setups add explicitly.\n\n**SWC side**: `crates/swc/src/lib.rs`'s doc comment states the guaranteed pass order \u2014 decorators are handled **before** the resolver and **before** TypeScript stripping \u2014 confirmed by `swc_ecma_transforms_typescript/src/{typescript,config}.rs` containing zero decorator-related logic or config fields; TS stripping is decorator-agnostic. The actual decorator pass lives in `swc_ecma_transforms_proposal/src/decorators/mod.rs`, which dispatches on `Config.legacy`/`Config.emit_metadata` to `decorators/legacy/mod.rs` (emits `_ts_decorate` calls) and, only when `emit_metadata` is set, `decorators/legacy/metadata.rs` (emits `Reflect.metadata`-driving `design:type`/`design:paramtypes`/`design:returntype` decorators).\n\n**The divergence** is wired in `crates/swc/src/config/mod.rs`: SWC silently defaults `transform.legacy_decorator = true` whenever `syntax.typescript()` is set, but `transform.decorator_metadata` has no such auto-default \u2014 it stays `false` unless the customer explicitly sets `jsc.transform.decoratorMetadata: true` in `.swcrc`. So a `.swcrc` that only sets `\"legacyDecorator\": true` (or relies on the TS-syntax auto-default) gets `@injectable()` classes decorated but with **no `Reflect.metadata` calls emitted at all**, while their old Babel config almost certainly paired `plugin-proposal-decorators` (legacy) with an explicit metadata-emitting plugin. NestJS's DI container reads `Reflect.getMetadata('design:paramtypes', ...)` at module-scan time; with no metadata ever attached, that call returns `undefined`, matching the reported crash.",
